 Security – Interview Questions

🔹 Kubernetes Architecture (Advanced)

• Explain Kubernetes control plane components in detail
• How does kube-apiserver handle authentication & authorization?
• Role of etcd in Kubernetes — why is it critical?
• What happens internally when you run kubectl apply?
• Scheduler decision process — how pods are scheduled?
• kube-controller-manager responsibilities
• How Kubernetes ensures high availability?

🔹 Cluster Design & Scalability

• Single vs multi-master cluster — differences
• Horizontal Pod Autoscaler vs Vertical Pod Autoscaler
• Cluster Autoscaler — how it works?
• Node pools — use cases
• When should you use multiple clusters?

🔹 Kubernetes Security (Interview Favorite)
• Kubernetes authentication mechanisms
• RBAC — roles vs cluster roles
• RoleBinding vs ClusterRoleBinding
• ServiceAccount — how it works?
• Pod Security Standards (Baseline, Restricted, Privileged)
• Network policies — why are they important?

🔹 Secrets & Configuration Security

• Secrets vs ConfigMaps
• Why Kubernetes Secrets are not truly encrypted by default?
• How to secure Secrets in production?
• External secrets — why & how?
• Mounting secrets as env vs volumes — which is safer?
🔹 Container Runtime & Node Security

• Docker vs containerd — differences
• Securing worker nodes
• Node compromise — detection & response
• kubelet security best practices

🔹 Production Incident Scenarios

• etcd failure — impact & recovery
• API server down — what happens to workloads?
• Unauthorized access to cluster — immediate actions?
• NetworkPolicy misconfiguration — troubleshooting steps
• Pod running as root — how to prevent?
Interview Tip:
If you explain architecture + security together, interviewers know you understand real production Kubernetes.
